   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Profit on the diagram"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "At the profit-maximising output $q_0$, total revenue is the rectangle $p \\times q_0$ and total cost is $AC(q_0) \\times q_0$. So profit $= (p - AC) \\times q_0$, the rectangle between the price line and the AC curve. If price is below AC but above AVC, the firm makes a loss but still produces in the short run. If p equals minimum AC, profit is zero (normal profit)."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Profit = (p − AC) × q₀"
    },
    {
     "en": "p > AC: super-normal profit; p = AC: normal profit; AVC < p < AC: loss but produce"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Profit on the diagram is the rectangle between the price line and the average cost curve, up to the chosen output.",
    "kn": "ಚಿತ್ರದಲ್ಲಿ ಲಾಭವು ಬೆಲೆ ರೇಖೆ ಮತ್ತು ಸರಾಸರಿ ವೆಚ್ಚ ವಕ್ರರೇಖೆಯ ನಡುವಿನ ಆಯತ, ಆಯ್ದ ಉತ್ಪನ್ನದವರೆಗೆ."
   },
   "formula": "\\pi = (p - AC)\\times q_0"
  },
